04:22:28 out   # VIDSYNC mechanics
04:22:28 out   This sheet lists the values that shape VIDSYNC. There is no original program to
04:22:28 out   compare against, so design choices are marked **estimated**. Values taken from
04:22:28 out   the person's requests are marked with that source; values read from Audacity on
04:22:28 out   the build machine are marked **observed**. The same values live in
04:22:28 out   [`mechanics.json`](mechanics.json).
04:22:28 out   VIDSYNC is a video player, not a game. "Mechanics" here means following
04:22:28 out   Audacity 4.0's timecode, playback, the status bar and the small settings panel.
04:22:28 out   ## Following Audacity
04:22:28 out   The person asked for a player with no transport of its own: Audacity 4.0's
04:22:28 out   timecode is the clock, the player is the slave, and the hierarchy of desktop
04:22:28 out   windows must not matter.
04:22:28 out   | Value | Setting | Source |
04:22:28 out   | --- | --- | --- |
04:22:28 out   | Timecode source | AT-SPI accessible name `Playback position:00 h 00 m 00.000 s`; any short name ending in a clock also works | observed (Audacity 4.0.2) / fallback |
04:22:28 out   | Timecode readout format | `HH:MM:SS.mmm`, e.g. `00:00:11.037` | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Required Audacity display | `00h00m00.000s` for a green dot | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Green dot | Audacity found and timecode uses the hour/minute/second display | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Red dot | Audacity not found, or its timecode uses another display | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Window order | irrelevant; no focus or key injection | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Timecode poll interval | `33 ms` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Movement window | `220 ms` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Movement threshold | `0.0005 s` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Timecode jump threshold | `0.4 s` (restart the decoder nearby) | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Still-frame refresh threshold | `0.02 s` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Audacity rediscovery interval | `12 s` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Failed discovery retry | `1 s` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Audacity version observed | `4.0.2` | observed (build machine) |
04:22:28 out   | Display server | any Linux desktop with AT-SPI, X11 or Wayland | observed / estimated |
04:22:28 out   The background thread walks the accessibility tree once, caches the node whose
04:22:28 out   name starts with `Playback position`, and reads it about thirty times a second.
04:22:28 out   A value that changes within the movement window marks Audacity as playing. The
04:22:28 out   UI then either follows the clock or holds a still frame. Nothing is sent to
04:22:28 out   Audacity and no window is raised, so the two applications can be stacked in any
04:22:28 out   order.
04:22:28 out   When Audacity is playing, VIDSYNC follows each reading. A drift of more than
04:22:28 out   `0.4 s` restarts `ffmpeg` from the new position; smaller drift is absorbed by
04:22:28 out   the decoder already running. When the clock stops changing, the decoder is
04:22:28 out   stopped and a still frame is fetched for the held position. If Audacity jumps
04:22:28 out   backwards, or its stop action returns the play head to zero, the picture follows
04:22:28 out   that jump.
04:22:28 out   ## Playback
04:22:28 out   | Value | Setting | Source |
04:22:28 out   | --- | --- | --- |
04:22:28 out   | Playback rate | `1.0x`, paced by the external timecode | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Output frame rate | `30 fps` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Maximum decoded width | `1280 px` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Maximum decoded height | `720 px` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Decoded frame queue | `12 frames` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Decoder channel buffer | `8 frames` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Longest accepted frame step | `0.1 s` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Audio output | none (audio streams are dropped) | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Supported formats | whatever the bundled `ffmpeg` can decode | user request |
04:22:28 out   Frames are decoded by `ffmpeg` to raw RGBA, scaled with bicubic filtering to fit
04:22:28 out   inside 1280x720 while preserving aspect ratio, and sampled at a fixed 30 fps.
04:22:28 out   The player displays the newest frame whose timestamp has been reached, so a slow
04:22:28 out   decode skips frames instead of slowing the follow. The image is letterboxed in
04:22:28 out   the window; it is never stretched.
04:22:28 out   `ffmpeg` decodes as fast as the machine allows, so the 12-frame queue keeps the
04:22:28 out   *earliest* frames and stops reading from the decoder while it is full. Draining
04:22:28 out   every available frame would throw away the pictures the clock is at and leave
04:22:28 out   only frames from seconds in the future. When Audacity runs past the end of a
04:22:28 out   short clip, the player parks on the last frame instead of restarting the
04:22:28 out   decoder on every timecode tick.
04:22:28 out   Audio, subtitles and data streams are explicitly dropped (`-an -sn -dn`). Video
04:22:28 out   codecs and containers are whatever the bundled/system `ffmpeg` can decode:
04:22:28 out   MP4, MKV, MOV, WebM, AVI, MPEG, TS, MTS, OGV, FLV, WMV and more.
04:22:28 out   ## Controls and transport
04:22:28 out   The person asked to remove the start-time field, the Audacity on/off switch and
04:22:28 out   the play, pause and record buttons. Audacity is the only transport.
04:22:28 out   | Value | Setting | Source |
04:22:28 out   | --- | --- | --- |
04:22:28 out   | Play button | none | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Pause button | none | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Record button | none | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Start-time field | none | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Audacity toggle switch | none | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Open shortcut | `O` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Fullscreen shortcut | `F` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Fullscreen button | header, beside the gear | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Exit fullscreen | `Escape` | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Close settings | `Escape` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | File loading | built-in browser only | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Drag and drop | none | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Empty-stage message | none; the stage stays black | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Sample-clip shortcut | none | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Keep-on-top setting | on/off switch in the settings panel | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Keep-on-top default | off | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Keep-on-top persistence | saved with mode and accent | estimated |
04:22:28 out   The header keeps only the wordmark, the current file name, an Open button, a
04:22:28 out   fullscreen button and the gear. The body is the picture and the status bar. With
04:22:28 out   no file loaded the body is an empty black stage with no text, icon or button.
04:22:28 out   The status bar keeps the `Audacity` label, its green/red dot and the
04:22:28 out   `00:00:00.000` readout. Fullscreen removes the header, status bar and every
04:22:28 out   other overlay; only the picture and its black letterbox/pillarbox remain.
04:22:28 out   ## Interface, layout and themes
04:22:28 out   | Value | Setting | Source |
04:22:28 out   | --- | --- | --- |
04:22:28 out   | Window size | `1120x720` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Video viewport margin | `0 px`; flush to the window sides, header and status bar | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Top bar height | `52 px` normal, `44 px` compact | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Status bar height | `70 px` normal, `58 px` compact | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Status bar side padding | `18 px` normal, `12 px` compact | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Timecode font | `32 px` normal, `22 px` compact, `18 px` narrow | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Timecode area width | `280 px` normal, `200 px` compact, `160 px` narrow | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Audacity label | `14 px` normal, `12 px` compact | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Status dot | `4.5 px` radius, with a glow while following | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Compact breakpoint | `880 px` window width | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Narrowest layout breakpoint | `500 px` window width | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Smallest tested window | `460x360` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Toast duration | `4.5 s` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | File browser double-click window | `0.38 s` | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Theme choices | `orange, yellow, green, blue, purple, red` | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Default theme | `purple` | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Interface modes | `dark, light` | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Default interface mode | `dark` | user request |
04:22:28 out   | Settings panel | `238x168 px` popover under the gear | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Settings panel swatch | `24 px`, spaced `34 px` apart | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Keep-on-top switch | `40x20 px`, on the right of its row | estimated |
04:22:28 out   | Keep-on-top row | full panel width, `28 px` high | estimated |
04:22:28 out   The layout switches to a compact status bar below 880 px wide: the bars get
04:22:28 out   shorter, the timecode drops to 22 px, the Audacity label drops to 12 px and the
04:22:28 out   side padding shrinks. Below 500 px the timecode drops to 18 px and its area
04:22:28 out   narrows to 160 px. The built-in file browser also drops its sidebar below
04:22:28 out   540 px and uses a smaller footer.
04:22:28 out   The gear opens a settings popover rather than a separate window. A Dark / Light
04:22:28 out   choice switches the whole interface; dark is the default. Choosing a swatch
04:22:28 out   changes every accent immediately: the brand mark, play icon, settings
04:22:28 out   highlights and folder highlights. The Keep on top switch adds or removes
04:22:28 out   `_NET_WM_STATE_ABOVE` on the player window. All three choices are saved to
04:22:28 out   `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vidsync/settings.json` and restored on the next launch, so a
04:22:28 out   missing file simply means dark, purple and not on top.
04:22:28 out   ## Sources and unknowns
04:22:28 out   - The latest request removes the empty-stage prompt, the sample-clip shortcut
04:22:28 out   and drag-and-drop: videos load only from the built-in browser. The settings
04:22:28 out   panel now also has a Keep on top switch, saved between launches.
04:22:28 out   - Earlier requests define the rest of this version: no transport buttons, no
04:22:28 out   start-time field, no Audacity switch, a live `00:00:00.000` readout, a
04:22:28 out   green/red dot for Audacity and its `00h00m00.000s` display, a minimalist slave
04:22:28 out   player, and window-order independence.
04:22:28 out   - Audacity 4.0.2 was running on the build machine. Its accessible tree exposes
04:22:28 out   the name `Playback position:00 h 00 m 00.000 s`, and the value advanced while
04:22:28 out   Audacity played. VIDSYNC's live trace followed it and reset with Audacity's
04:22:28 out   stop-to-zero.
04:22:28 out   - Audacity 4.0 on other Linux desktops, and any future Audacity version, could
04:22:28 out   expose a different accessible name. VIDSYNC falls back to any short accessible
04:22:28 out   name that ends in a clock, so translated labels work, but a future release
04:22:28 out   could change the clock format itself.
04:22:28 out   - The accessibility bus must be running. VIDSYNC switches `IsEnabled` on, but
04:22:28 out   cannot install a missing AT-SPI stack.
04:22:28 out   - Every numeric layout value is a design choice for this build, not a copied
04:22:28 out   constant.
04:22:28 out   - Decode size and frame rate trade sharpness for CPU and memory; they can be
04:22:28 out   changed in `src/player.rs` and kept in step with `mechanics.json`.
