04:23:07 out   //! Audacity 4.0 timecode from the desktop accessibility layer.
04:23:07 out   //!
04:23:07 out   //! On Linux, Audacity 4.0 is a Qt application that publishes its playback
04:23:07 out   //! position as an AT-SPI accessible name (`Playback position:00 h 00 m 11.037
04:23:07 out   //! s`). On Windows the same Qt accessibility tree is exposed through UI
04:23:07 out   //! Automation (UIA); the accessible Name (or the Value pattern) carries the
04:23:07 out   //! same text.
04:23:07 out   //!
04:23:07 out   //! Either way a background thread discovers the Audacity accessible tree,
04:23:07 out   //! caches the node that holds the timecode, and polls it about thirty times a
04:23:07 out   //! second. The UI only reads a small snapshot, so a slow or missing Audacity
04:23:07 out   //! never stalls the video.
